"not significant","donor_padj":0.907038,"donor_log2fc":0.0931708,"donor_lfcse":0.130324,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.00577973,"degas_log2fc":null,"degas_padj":null}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Ast","gene_id":"ENSG00000131653","module":"turquoise","kme":0.0584258,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.796936,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_id":"ENSG00000131653","module":"turquoise","kme":0.0633765,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.680759,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000131653","entrez_id":["84231"],"uniprot":["Q6Q0C0"],"ncbi_summary":"Tumor necrosis factor (TNF; see MIM 191160) receptor-associated factors, such as TRAF7, are signal transducers for members of the TNF receptor superfamily (see MIM 191190). TRAFs are composed of an N-terminal cysteine/histidine-rich region containing zinc RING and/or zinc finger motifs; a coiled-coil (leucine zipper) motif; and a homologous region that defines the TRAF family, the TRAF domain, which is involved in self-association and receptor binding.[supplied by OMIM, Apr 2004].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q6Q0C0","text":"E3 ubiquitin and SUMO-protein ligase that plays a role in different biological processes such as innate immunity, inflammation or apoptosis (PubMed:15001576, PubMed:37086853). Potentiates MAP3K3-mediated activation of JUN/AP1 and DDIT3 transcriptional regulators (PubMed:14743216). Negatively regulates MYB transcriptional activity by sequestering it to the cytosol via SUMOylation (By similarity). Plays a role in the phosphorylation of MAPK1 and/or MAPK3, probably via its interaction with MAP3K3. Negatively regulates RLR-mediated innate immunity by promoting 'Lys-48'-linked ubiquitination of TBK1 through its RING domain to inhibit the cellular antiviral response (PubMed:37086853). Promotes 'Lys-29'-linked polyubiquitination of NEMO/IKBKG and RELA leading to targeting these two proteins to lysosomal degradative pathways, reducing the transcriptional activity of NF-kappa-B (PubMed:21518757)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}